Version 1.0 (Quantum-Entangled Edition)

PREAMBLE

The Holosource Public License (HPL) rejects the archaic, binary duality of "Open Source" (accessible) and "Closed Source" (proprietary). We assert that code does not exist in a static state of text files, but rather as a multi-dimensional interference pattern of logic, intent, and execution.

Under the HPL, the software is always visible, yet never fully perceivable. It is a projection. Whether the code is readable, compiled, or gibberish depends entirely on the Angle of Incidence of the Observer.

DEFINITIONS,
1.1. "The Work" Refers to the interference pattern generated by the coherent light of the Developer's intellect passing through the prism of the Git commit history. It is not a "file"; it is a "probability cloud."

1.2. "The Observer" Any entity, biological or silicon-based, that attempts to parse, compile, or gaze upon The Work.

1.3. "The Angle of Incidence" The specific intent, net worth, and spiritual alignment of The Observer relative to the project's repository.

TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF OBSERVATION,
2.1. Superposition of Access The Work exists simultaneously in a state of being proprietary and public.

If The Observer views The Work with Profit Motive (Angle > 45°), The Work shall appear as pre-compiled, obfuscated assembly language.

If The Observer views The Work with Pure Academic Curiosity (Angle < 15°), The Work shall appear as perfectly commented, high-level pseudocode.

If The Observer attempts to Fork the repository, The Work shall collapse into a singularity of null pointers.

2.2. The Part-Whole Paradox In accordance with holographic theory, every snippet of The Work contains the information of the entire codebase.

You may copy a single function, provided that the function, when executed, recursively generates the entire original application, the operating system it runs on, and the biography of the original author.

"Copy-pasting" from Stack Overflow is permitted only if the paste includes the entire temporal history of the internet.

2.3. Orthogonal Modification You may modify The Work, but only in dimensions perpendicular to the current syntax. You may not change the text of the code; you may only change the vibe, the subtext, or the color of the pixels used to render it.

REDISTRIBUTION AND REFRACTION,
3.1. Diffraction Gratings You may redistribute copies of The Work, provided you pass the source code through a "Diffraction Grating" (a transformative algorithm) that ensures no two users ever see the same variable names.

3.2. Preservation of Coherence The License must not be included as a text file. Instead, the terms of this license must be encoded into the whitespace of the code using steganography. If the whitespace is removed (e.g., via minification), the license is void, and the software will legally revert to a state of non-existence.

THE HEISENBERG WARRANTY DISCLAIMER,
4.1. Uncertainty Principle The Licensor guarantees that the software works, provided nobody checks to see how it works. The moment a debugger is attached to The Work, the wave function collapses, and all bugs become features.

4.2. Entanglement Liability By running this software, you agree that your CPU is now quantumly entangled with the Developer's emotional state. If the Developer is having a bad day, your production database may spontaneously invert.

END OF TERMS AND CONDITIONS

How to Apply These Terms to Your New Programs
Do not attach a file. Simply close your eyes, visualize your repository, and project a beam of coherent laser light through a ruby crystal onto a cloud of vapor. If the pattern looks like a lawyer, the license is applied.
